# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2.1 Stripe  (apps/api, apps/web, packages/auth, packages/trpc)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BREAKS: the better-auth stripe plugin loads but every Stripe API call 401s.
# CONCRETE RISK, verified at packages/auth/src/server.ts:490-505 —
# `afterCreateOrganization` calls stripeClient.customers.create() whenever
# NODE_ENV !== "development", and it is NOT wrapped in try/catch. Creating an
# organization through the API therefore throws in production.
# Your three orgs come from `bun run db:seed-teams`, which INSERTs orgs
# directly (db.insert(organizations)) and bypasses that hook — but the same
# script's signUpEmail triggers the user-create hook, whose personal-org
# fallback (server.ts:241-249) DOES call auth.api.createOrganization.
# MITIGATION: run the seed with NODE_ENV=development, mirroring the existing
# `db:seed-dev` script:
#   NODE_ENV=development SUPERSET_ALLOW_SIGNUP=true SEED_TEAMS_CONFIRM=yes bun run db:seed-teams
# Afterwards, self-serve org creation in the UI will still fail. Accepted:
# this instance has exactly three orgs, all seeded.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_unused_selfhosted
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_unused_selfhosted
STRIPE_PRO_MONTHLY_PRICE_ID=price_unused_pro_monthly
STRIPE_PRO_YEARLY_PRICE_ID=price_unused_pro_yearly
# Required by packages/auth/src/env.ts only (not by apps/api).
STRIPE_ENTERPRISE_YEARLY_PRICE_ID=price_unused_enterprise_yearly

