# #############################################################################
# BUILD TIME vs RUNTIME
# #############################################################################
#
# THE BUILD COMMAND ITSELF — turbo strips env vars it was not told about.
#    turbo 2.10.9 (package.json) defaults to STRICT env mode, and turbo.jsonc
#    declares no `envMode`. Its globalEnv list does NOT contain RELAY_URL,
#    NEXT_PUBLIC_RELAY_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_COOKIE_DOMAIN or BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, so
#    a plain `turbo build` hands `next build` an environment with those removed
#    — producing exactly the broken CSP described under (A) below, from an
#    otherwise correct .env. Build with the environment exported AND loose mode:
#
#      cd <repo root>
#      set -a; . ./.env; set +a
#      bunx turbo build --filter=@superset/api --filter=@superset/web --env-mode=loose
#
#    (`next build` forces NODE_ENV=production, so apps/{api,web}/next.config.ts
#     skip their dotenv load of ../../.env — exporting it first is required, not
#     optional. The root `build` script is `turbo build --filter=@superset/desktop`
#     and does NOT build api or web.)
#
# A) apps/web + apps/api — BUILD TIME (`next build` on ms1)
#    Next.js inlines every NEXT_PUBLIC_* into the client bundle at build. A
#    change to any of these needs a REBUILD, not a restart:
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_RELAY_URL,
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_MARKETING_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_DOCS_URL,
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_COOKIE_DOMAIN, NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY,
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST, NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_*, NEXT_PUBLIC_DESKTOP_URL
#
#    Plus two NON-public vars that apps/web/next.config.ts reads while building
#    the Content-Security-Policy header:
#      RELAY_URL         -> connect-src wss:// + https:// relay origins.
#                           If it is missing at build time and NODE_ENV is
#                           production, the CSP hardcodes wss://relay.superset.sh
#                           and the browser will BLOCK your relay WebSocket.
#                           This is the single easiest way to break terminals.
#      RELAY_BACKUP_URL  -> optional extra origin (see section 3).
#
#    Everything else in sections 1-2 is RUNTIME: read from process.env by the
#    running `next start` / relay process. Changing them needs only a restart.
#
# B) apps/relay — RUNTIME only. It is a plain Bun process; every value in
#    apps/relay/src/env.ts is read from process.env at boot. No build step.
#    Remember `bun run src/index.ts` does not load .env — export the vars.
#
# C) apps/desktop — BUILD TIME (apps/desktop/electron.vite.config.ts `define:`)
#    These are string-substituted into the Electron bundle. Their fallbacks all
#    point at Superset's HOSTED service, so a desktop build that does not set
#    them will silently talk to api.superset.sh instead of your instance:
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL        (fallback https://api.superset.sh)
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB_URL        (fallback https://app.superset.sh)
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_MARKETING_URL  (fallback https://superset.sh)
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_DOCS_URL       (fallback https://docs.superset.sh)
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_ROOT_DOMAIN    (fallback superset.sh)
#      RELAY_URL                  (no fallback in the define; env.main.ts
#                                  schema default is https://relay.superset.sh)
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_STREAMS_URL    (fallback https://streams.superset.sh)
#      STREAMS_URL                (fallback https://superset-stream.fly.dev)
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY, NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST
#      SENTRY_DSN_DESKTOP, SENTRY_DSN_HOST_SERVICE
#      NODE_ENV, SKIP_ENV_VALIDATION
#      DESKTOP_VITE_PORT, DESKTOP_NOTIFICATIONS_PORT, SUPERSET_WORKSPACE_NAME
#                                  (dev-only ports / labels)
#
#    apps/desktop/src/main/env.main.ts sets `skipValidation` to true ONLY when
#    NODE_ENV === "development" AND SKIP_ENV_VALIDATION is set — a production
#    desktop build always validates. Every var above has a schema default, so
#    validation still passes; the risk is a silently-wrong default, not a crash.
#
#    UNVERIFIED: whether the desktop app needs a working STREAMS_URL /
#    NEXT_PUBLIC_STREAMS_URL for this deployment. apps/streams exists in the
#    repo but is not in the stated deployment scope, and the defaults point at
#    Superset-hosted endpoints. Decide this before shipping a desktop build.
#
# D) Migrations — run once on ms1 before first boot, with DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED
#    exported:  bun run db:push     (or: bun run db:migrate)
#    drizzle-kit is the ONLY consumer of DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED.
